1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:01,660
Welcome.

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:11,848
In this tutorial you will learn which database
to install for the DEIHS Maintenance
Management System, and how to connect the application to it.

3
00:00:12,028 --> 00:00:20,428
We will use XAMPP, import the included SQL
script, edit the connection settings, and run
the app.

4
00:00:20,608 --> 00:00:21,808
Let's begin.

5
00:00:23,408 --> 00:00:26,480
Here is the whole setup in five steps.

6
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:33,356
First, install XAMPP so you have a
MySQL-compatible database server.

7
00:00:33,536 --> 00:00:37,280
Second, import the schema that comes with the
project.

8
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:40,340
Third, point the app at your database.

9
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:43,328
Fourth, build and run the application.

10
00:00:43,508 --> 00:00:49,964
And fifth, if you are on a local network,
connect the other computers to the same
database.

11
00:00:51,564 --> 00:00:54,996
Before you start, prepare these four things.

12
00:00:55,176 --> 00:00:59,376
A computer running Windows, macOS, or Linux.

13
00:00:59,556 --> 00:01:02,940
The Java Development Kit version twenty-one.

14
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:07,152
Apache Maven, which is only needed to build
the project.

15
00:01:07,332 --> 00:01:12,852
And the project folder itself, which you can
download or clone from GitHub.

16
00:01:13,032 --> 00:01:16,896
You will also need a web browser for
phpMyAdmin.

17
00:01:18,496 --> 00:01:22,480
The application works with MySQL or MariaDB.

18
00:01:22,660 --> 00:01:32,644
The easiest choice for members is XAMPP,
because it bundles MariaDB, Apache, and
phpMyAdmin in one installer.

19
00:01:32,824 --> 00:01:42,160
MariaDB speaks the same protocol as MySQL, so
the MySQL Connector included in the project
works without changes.

20
00:01:42,340 --> 00:01:48,004
If your school already runs MySQL 8 or WAMP,
you can use that instead.

21
00:01:49,604 --> 00:01:56,948
Download XAMPP from apachefriends dot org and
choose the version for your operating system.

22
00:01:57,128 --> 00:02:05,072
Run the installer and keep the default
location, which is C colon backslash xampp on
Windows.

23
00:02:05,252 --> 00:02:12,740
You do not need every component, but keep
Apache, MySQL, and phpMyAdmin selected.

24
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:18,296
When installation finishes, open the XAMPP
Control Panel.

25
00:02:19,896 --> 00:02:27,120
In the XAMPP Control Panel, click Start next
to Apache and Start next to MySQL.

26
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:30,444
Both should turn green and show a port number.

27
00:02:30,624 --> 00:02:35,040
MySQL normally listens on port three three
zero six.

28
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:42,540
If the port is already in use, another
database is running, and you will need to stop
it or change the port.

29
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:45,768
Leave both services running while you work.

30
00:02:47,368 --> 00:02:51,784
If you do not have the project yet, clone it
from GitHub.

31
00:02:51,964 --> 00:03:00,364
Open a terminal in the folder where you keep
your projects and run git clone with the
repository URL shown on screen.

32
00:03:00,544 --> 00:03:06,568
If Git is not installed, you can download the
repository as a ZIP file instead.

33
00:03:06,748 --> 00:03:10,564
The next video covers GitHub access in detail.

34
00:03:12,164 --> 00:03:17,468
phpMyAdmin is the web interface that comes
with XAMPP.

35
00:03:17,648 --> 00:03:25,160
With Apache and MySQL running, open your
browser and go to localhost slash phpmyadmin.

36
00:03:25,340 --> 00:03:28,676
You should see the phpMyAdmin home page.

37
00:03:28,856 --> 00:03:36,584
On a fresh XAMPP install, the user is root and
the password is blank, so you can log in
directly.

38
00:03:38,184 --> 00:03:41,712
In phpMyAdmin, click the Import tab.

39
00:03:41,892 --> 00:03:51,156
Choose the file database slash deihs mms dot s
q l from the project folder, leave the default
options, and click Go.

40
00:03:51,336 --> 00:03:57,192
The script creates the database, all thirteen
tables, and the demo accounts.

41
00:03:57,372 --> 00:03:59,820
Please read the warning on screen.

42
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:07,056
The script begins with drop database, so it
replaces any existing database with the same
name.

43
00:04:08,656 --> 00:04:14,296
After the import, phpMyAdmin should show the
new database on the left.

44
00:04:14,476 --> 00:04:17,572
Open it and confirm that the tables are there.

45
00:04:17,752 --> 00:04:26,896
You should see tables for users, requests,
facilities, equipment, schedules, and the
audit log, among others.

46
00:04:27,076 --> 00:04:33,196
If the import failed, check the error message
at the top of the page before continuing.

47
00:04:34,796 --> 00:04:38,492
Now tell the application how to reach the
database.

48
00:04:38,672 --> 00:04:46,064
Open src slash main slash resources slash db
dot properties in any text editor.

49
00:04:46,244 --> 00:04:57,596
Set the host to one two seven dot zero dot
zero dot one, the port to three three zero
six, the database name to deihs mms, and the user to root.

50
00:04:57,776 --> 00:05:02,960
Leave the password blank only for a local
XAMPP install.

51
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:08,760
This step causes the most confusion, so pay
attention.

52
00:05:08,940 --> 00:05:18,732
The copy of db dot properties stored in the
repository uses port three three zero seven,
because that was the developer's local setup.

53
00:05:18,912 --> 00:05:24,216
XAMPP uses port three three zero six by
default.

54
00:05:24,396 --> 00:05:29,580
If you keep three three zero seven, the
application cannot connect.

55
00:05:29,760 --> 00:05:35,856
Change the port to three three zero six unless
you deliberately configured a different one.

56
00:05:37,456 --> 00:05:43,888
Using root with a blank password is fine for a
quick test, but not for a shared deployment.

57
00:05:44,068 --> 00:05:49,204
Create a dedicated database user that can
access only this database.

58
00:05:49,384 --> 00:05:52,360
The SQL commands are shown on screen.

59
00:05:52,540 --> 00:06:00,556
Replace the password with a strong one, and
put the same credentials in db dot properties
or pass them at launch.

60
00:06:02,156 --> 00:06:05,132
Open a terminal in the project folder.

61
00:06:05,312 --> 00:06:10,592
Run mvn clean package to compile and package
the application.

62
00:06:10,772 --> 00:06:20,372
When the build finishes, start it with java
dash jar target slash deihs dash mms dash one
dot zero dot zero dot jar.

63
00:06:20,552 --> 00:06:28,832
On Linux or macOS you can also run the
provided run dot s h script, and on Windows
use run dot b a t.

64
00:06:30,432 --> 00:06:34,224
When the login screen appears, the connection
is working.

65
00:06:34,404 --> 00:06:42,444
Sign in with one of the demo accounts listed
in the README, for example admin with password
admin one two three.

66
00:06:42,624 --> 00:06:47,016
Change the demo passwords before anyone else
uses the system.

67
00:06:47,196 --> 00:06:55,764
If the login screen shows a connection error,
the problem is almost always the host, port,
user, or password.

68
00:06:57,364 --> 00:07:03,316
To share one database across several
computers, start with the server PC.

69
00:07:03,496 --> 00:07:10,024
Find its local IP address with ipconfig on
Windows or ip address on Linux.

70
00:07:10,204 --> 00:07:15,820
Allow inbound TCP port three three zero six
through the firewall.

71
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:23,224
In MySQL, make sure the user is allowed to
connect from the network, not only from
localhost.

72
00:07:23,404 --> 00:07:26,260
Then import the schema on that machine.

73
00:07:27,860 --> 00:07:33,980
On each client PC, install Java twenty-one and
copy the packaged jar.

74
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:42,896
Start it with db dot host set to the server's
IP address and db dot port set to three three
zero six, as shown.

75
00:07:43,076 --> 00:07:47,396
Alternatively, edit db dot properties on that
PC.

76
00:07:47,576 --> 00:07:53,360
All computers then read and write the same
data, so changes appear everywhere.

77
00:07:54,960 --> 00:07:58,392
Here are the four errors you are most likely
to see.

78
00:07:58,572 --> 00:08:05,724
Access denied means the username or password
is wrong, or the user is not allowed from that
host.

79
00:08:05,904 --> 00:08:12,648
Communications link failure means the host or
port is wrong, or MySQL is not running.

80
00:08:12,828 --> 00:08:16,596
Unknown database means the import did not
complete.

81
00:08:16,776 --> 00:08:22,920
And a port conflict means another service is
already using three three zero six.

82
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:27,904
Before real use, do these four things.

83
00:08:28,084 --> 00:08:30,292
Change every demo password.

84
00:08:30,472 --> 00:08:34,600
Create a dedicated database user instead of
using root.

85
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:39,460
Never expose port three three zero six
directly to the internet.

86
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:42,904
And never commit real passwords to GitHub.

87
00:08:43,084 --> 00:08:48,028
Pass them at launch, or keep them in a local
file that is not tracked.

88
00:08:49,628 --> 00:08:52,292
That completes the database setup.

89
00:08:52,472 --> 00:09:00,248
You installed XAMPP, imported the schema,
configured the connection, and ran the
application.

90
00:09:00,428 --> 00:09:07,964
If something did not work, revisit the
troubleshooting slide, and check the README
for the same steps in writing.

91
00:09:08,144 --> 00:09:13,664
In the next video, we will cover how to access
the GitHub repository.
